#: src/android/interoperability/with-c.md:38
msgid ""
"The [`\"C\"` part](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/items/external-blocks."
"html#abi) of the `extern` block tells Rust that `abs` can be called using "
"the C [ABI](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Application_binary_interface) "
"(application binary interface)."
msgstr ""

#: src/android/interoperability/with-c.md:41
msgid ""
"The `safe fn abs` part tells Rust that `abs` is a safe function. By default, "
"extern functions are unsafe, but since `abs(x)` can't trigger undefined "
"behavior with any `x`, we can declare it safe."
msgstr ""
